WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:03.269
[music playing]

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:08.141
NARRATOR: Day breaks over
the lovely forested south rim

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:13.713
of the canyon lighting
up a dead pine that would

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:16.583
seem to have little purpose.

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:19.953
But this pine is the
central bank and trust

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:23.123
of the acorn woodpecker.

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:25.492
And every inch is
studded with neatly

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:31.464
arranged holes, the
woodpecker's safe deposit boxes.

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:35.335
Finding the absolutely perfect
little vault for every acorn

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:37.404
can be quite the puzzle.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:41.207
Each hole has been drilled
to fit a certain nut shape.

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:44.677
[bird calls]

00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:54.454
Keeping the treasure
house secure

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:58.158
requires a bonding of the
birds, a breeding collective

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.427
of several males
and females along

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:05.198
with their extended family who
make deposits and stand guard.

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:08.168
[bird calls]

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:12.238
[music playing]

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:24.784
They can be little
gymnasts when threats come

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:27.921
from above simply skittering
to the underside of the bank

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:28.721
branches.

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:36.362
This is just a false
alarm though, a raven,

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:37.897
the jokester of the canyon.

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:49.576
There are far more serious
threats from below.

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:53.246
Squirrels know exactly how the
woodpecker banks work and are

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:54.914
always casing the joint.

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:00.053
And who could blame him.

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:02.355
Just look at all those acorns.

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:05.692
This squirrel believes
in sharing the wealth.

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:08.361
But he better eat fast
and stuff those cheeks.

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:15.368
[bird calls]

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:18.371
The woodpecker bank
tellers hit the alarm.

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:25.945
And the security guards
swing into action.

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:29.449
[music playing]

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:58.011
The bank is secured
again, but it

00:02:58.077 --> 00:03:00.647
won't be long before
the habitual thief

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:03.149
tries another stickup.

